From: WG2600HP IPQ8064 isolated candidate
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: 8021q: unwind partial registration before freeing context

Linux baseline: v6.12.112; apply after the staged 760-03 tag_8021q dual-CPU isolation patch.

Failure in dsa_tag_8021q_setup() can occur after prior user ports
have installed VLAN membership and conduit RX filters. A bare kfree()
leaves ds->tag_8021q_ctx dangling and leaks partial hardware state.
Use the existing unregister path to undo programming and release the
context. Revalidation of failure cleanup on WG2600HP is required.
Staging only: not integrated, compiled or tested on hardware.

---
--- a/net/dsa/tag_8021q.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_8021q.c
@@ -445,7 +445,10 @@
 	return 0;
 
 err_free:
-	kfree(ctx);
+	/* Setup can fail after some ports have been programmed. Unwind their
+	 * VLANs, release the context and clear ds->tag_8021q_ctx.
+	 */
+	dsa_tag_8021q_unregister(ds);
 	return err;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dsa_tag_8021q_register);
